# Copy to .env and fill in what you need. NEVER commit .env — it is git-ignored,
# and CI fails the build outright if it is ever tracked (see SECURITY.md).
#
# Everything here is for LOCAL development and the offline pipeline. Deployed
# environments never read .env: those credentials live in SSM Parameter Store as
# SST secrets.
#
#   npx sst secret set SearchApiKey    <value> --stage <stage>
#   npx sst secret set AnthropicApiKey <value> --stage <stage>
#   npx sst secret list --stage <stage>
#
# --stage is not optional in practice. Without it SST writes to your personal
# stage, so a secret you believe you set on production is sitting somewhere
# else. List it back to check.
#
# Neither SST secret is needed to SERVE the site. SearchApiKey is linked only to
# the SQS crawl fetcher and AnthropicApiKey only to the classifier — both
# offline batch Lambdas — and nothing under packages/web reads either. A deploy
# with both unset succeeds and every page renders.

# --- the pipeline (local CLIs) ---

# https://www.searchapi.io/ — Maps engine credits.
# Read by: pnpm crawl, pnpm reviews, pnpm demand. Spending happens here, not in
# the cloud, which is why the local copy is the one that matters today.
SEARCH_API_KEY=

# https://console.anthropic.com/ — taxonomy classification (Haiku 4.5 + Batch API).
# Read by: pnpm classify.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- optional ---

# Which city config the site and its data bundler use. Default: dubai.
# A city is data, not code — see docs/adr/0005-toolkit-not-directory.md.
# DIRECTORY_CITY=dubai

# DynamoDB table for `pnpm load --yes`. Take it from the `table` output of
# `npx sst deploy`. A dry run does not need it.
# DIRECTORY_TABLE=

# Private S3 prefix the built dataset travels through, so CI can build without
# the dataset ever entering git. Read by pnpm dataset:push / dataset:pull.
# In CI this comes from the repository variable of the same name.
# See docs/adr/0015-ship-the-dataset-to-ci-through-private-s3.md
# DATASET_S3_URI=s3://<bucket>/<city>

# Region for the AWS SDK clients the pipeline uses (pnpm load, dataset:*).
# This does NOT move the deployed stack: sst.config.ts pins the provider to
# us-east-1 in code — see docs/adr/0003-deploy-region.md.
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# --- dev tooling only (not read by the pipeline) ---
# MCP access to SearchApi from Claude Code / Cursor (server name: dubai_directory).
# This is NOT the same value as SEARCH_API_KEY — generate a separate MCP
# token at https://www.searchapi.io/mcp_integrations
# Only needed for headless/CI use; interactive clients use OAuth instead.
# SEARCHAPI_MCP_TOKEN=
